{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1069950-mage-fortifications-and-defenses","id":1069950,"title":"Mage: fortifications and defenses","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-03-29T03:16:27-07:00","id":1069950,"title":"Mage: fortifications and defenses","content":"I would like some help with developing NPC defenses.<br /> <br /> How do mages fortify their properties or estates?<br /> <br /> I would assume they might have something act as sentry or protector, but are there any things I should consider? I don't want to make the NPCs seem sloppy or simple by avoiding heavy fortification, but I also don't want to make it an impossible gauntlet.<br /> <br /> For example: <br /> <br /> A gentleman's club guarded by various spirits (3) under the servitude of an adept ... but nothing else. The spirits are thematically related to different aspects of the club and are largely meant to turn the players around or sedate - is this appropriate for an NPC or is it too lackadaisal?<br /> <br /> I was wondering if I should toss in some sleepwalkers or even a single bonafide mage.<br /> <br /> I mostly want to know if I, more or less, have full discretion regarding defense (as complicated or utterly lacking as i want) or if mages are likely to resort to a common set of tactics. Something like &quot;Most mages will use some level of misdirection or veiling but won't bother with brute force enforcement unless the location really warrants it.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">N/A</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11166-kryptonitekrusher","name":"kryptonitekrusher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"200"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-29T03:30:04-07:00","id":1069952,"title":"","content":"The two most common defenses of a Sanctum are a Ward to protect from Sympathy and a Veil to mask its location (Though probably more from Sleepers than Mages). Anything beyond that depends on the resources available to the Mage(s) in question and their willingness to invest in defense. Playing to stereotype and not saying it's always the case Arrow, Mysterium are probably the most likely to go in for heavy defensive measures, Guardians are probably up there too but preferring misdirection and mundane layers of defense, the FC varies and probably relies on mundane security measures with a light overlay of magic, the SL are probably much the same but add an intimidation factor because they're backed by the Lex.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-31T09:40:19-07:00","id":1071297,"title":"","content":"I really like the club bouncer spirits idea. That seems perfectly appropriate to me. Two threads I started in the recent past might help you.<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1016963-magical-home-defence-101-tips-tricks-and-ideas\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1016963-magical-home-defence-101-tips-tricks-and-ideas\"> Magical Home Defence 101. Tips Tricks and Ideas. - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1016963-magical-home-defence-101-tips-tricks-and-ideas\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1016963-magical-home-defence-101-tips-tricks-and-ideas </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Imagine if you will that your enterprising young Cabal has come into possession of a charming new sanctum. The location is important for a few reasons, a previously </div> </div> </div><br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1066206-how-paranoid-are-your-mages\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1066206-how-paranoid-are-your-mages\"> How paranoid are your mages? - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1066206-how-paranoid-are-your-mages\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1066206-how-paranoid-are-your-mages </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> I am curious about the breadth of experience across the forum on this issue. For some their seems to often be an unspoken assumption that Mages refuse to leave their homes without casting a bevy of protective or divination spells first in the safety of their magically fortified nuclear bunker sanctums. On the one hand I can totally understand this view. Mages are relatively fragile compared to vampires or werewolves and are incredibly aware of how terrifyingly dangerous the world they live in is. If you had all this magic at your disposal, why wouldn't you take steps to protect yourself? On the other </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> The general rule in my book is that the level of defence can vary massively, depending on the personality of the Mage, some may like to take their chances, others cant sleep without a dozen wards between them and danger. Throw some NPCs of both extremes in your game, with the rest being somewhere in between.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6230-katana1515","name":"Katana1515","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6230_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-31T09:59:45-07:00","id":1071303,"title":"","content":"Utilizing the asymmetrical nature of Arcana is often your best bet.Shifting important bits of your Sanctum to Death Twilight is a great choice for a Death Mage, for example. Make accessing/navigating the placed without ability to cast your strongest Arcanum as impossible as possible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-31T10:15:00-07:00","id":1071308,"title":"","content":"I imagine you could do a Forces spell bound up with a Fate condition of &quot;When an unwelcome intruder enters this room&quot; to say... send out a phone call or text message to a group of people. Sure, it'll maybe take time to get there or they'll have to use Space to scry perhaps... but knowing IS half the battle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />\u200bWhen noise turns to silence, when colors dull and pale, when reality no longer makes sense, there shall you find me. There, in the dreams of the River of Faceless Millions, do I dwell.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/\" target=\"_blank\">http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/</a> for my art.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/378-haren","name":"haren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar378_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"664"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-31T11:09:25-07:00","id":1071330,"title":"","content":"Or you could just get a video stream up and set up some notification system for &quot;things enter, I know, camera shows me&quot; and potentially blast the person while looking at your iphone, no sympathy needed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}